// Result of evaluating a cluster's upgrade readiness. Returned by the
// upgrade_eligibility sub-resource of a cluster.
//
// All evaluation is performed server-side. Clients should treat this as
// advisory — it reflects OCM-visible state at the time of the request and
// does not guarantee that an upgrade scheduling call will succeed.
class UpgradeEligibility {
    // Eligible indicates whether the cluster passed all eligibility checks.
    // False when one or more findings with severity Blocker are present.
    Eligible Boolean

    // TargetVersion is the specific version that was checked, when provided
    // by the caller. Empty when the check evaluated general availability.
    TargetVersion String

    // AvailableUpgrades lists the upgrade targets available for this cluster,
    // filtered by product (HCP or Classic) as appropriate.
    AvailableUpgrades []String

    // Findings lists the individual evaluation results, ordered from most
    // severe to least severe.
    Findings []UpgradeEligibilityFinding

    // Gates lists the version gates relevant for the minor-version transition
    // implied by the target, with acknowledgement status per cluster.
    // Empty for z-stream (patch-only) upgrades.
    Gates []UpgradeEligibilityGate

    // EvaluatedAt is the timestamp when this evaluation was performed.
    EvaluatedAt Date
}
